    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99-a2">

                <pb facs="0271" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg143"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                        429.—Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Zelaya to Mr.
                            Hall</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 10,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Minister <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. C. Hall</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Guatemala:</hi></p>
                <p>I thank your Government, in behalf of my own, for the interest it takes in favor
                    of Honduras, by dictating opportune measures to impede the departure of any
                    filibustering expedition against her.</p>
                <p>This rectitude of conduct on the part of your Government will not only favor the
                    natives of this country who are engaged in peaceful labors, but it will
                    encourage the important North American enterprises, which rely for their success
                    upon the good order and tranquillity which the Republic now enjoys, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>JERONIMO ZELAYA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
